    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">ADVANCE FOR USE SUNDAY, OCT. 23, 2016 AND THEREAFTER - In this Sept. 22, 2016 photo, Alberto Olvera-Ocampo hands out maps during his  speech at a meeting of the Toastmasters in Sterling, Ill. The night was Olvera-Ocampo's ice-breaker speech, the first one he's delivered after joining the club two weeks back. The men and women of Toastmasters work to become more competent communicators, improve their listening skills, and learn the importance of speech "icebreakers" and visual aids. (Alex T. Paschal/Sauk Valley Media via AP)</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <dc:creator>
    <rdf:Seq>
     <rdf:li>Alex T. Paschal</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq>
   </dc:creator>
   <dc:title>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Exchange Helping Communication</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:title>
