     <rdf:li>AFP</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq>
   </dc:creator>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">TO GO WITH AFP STORY BY MIRA OBERMAN "US-CLIMATE-WARMING-TECHNOLOGY-ENERGY"&#xA;Chief engineer Ryan Egan demonstrates a new smart thermostat system installed at Chicago's riverside Sheraton hotel which will cut energy bills by $136,000 a year on November 29, 2012 in Chicago. Chicago's skyline is going green, as property managers install energy efficient tools like motion-detectors on office lights, in a project officials hope will inspire changes across the United States.   AFP PHOTO/MIRA OBERMAN        (Photo credit should read MIRA OBERMAN/AFP/Getty Images)</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <dc:subject>
